1
00:00:00,161 --> 00:00:02,216
See this line on a Google ad

2
00:00:02,236 --> 00:00:04,292
Customers love fresh bread

3
00:00:04,312 --> 00:00:05,950
The bakery didn't write that

4
00:00:06,028 --> 00:00:07,336
Google's AI did

5
00:00:07,504 --> 00:00:09,619
Google's own help page confirms it

6
00:00:09,639 --> 00:00:12,343
It's live in India the US the UK

7
00:00:12,363 --> 00:00:13,411
and Australia

8
00:00:13,506 --> 00:00:14,618
Here's how it works

9
00:00:14,638 --> 00:00:17,684
Google's AI reads a business's reviews from across

10
00:00:17,704 --> 00:00:18,517
the web

11
00:00:18,577 --> 00:00:20,675
and writes one line into its ad

12
00:00:20,761 --> 00:00:21,625
The catch

13
00:00:21,645 --> 00:00:23,618
It only uses the good reviews

14
00:00:23,638 --> 00:00:25,206
The bad ones never make it in

15
00:00:25,349 --> 00:00:27,294
And the business can't edit that line

16
00:00:27,428 --> 00:00:29,353
So when you search that line is part

17
00:00:29,373 --> 00:00:30,132
of an ad

18
00:00:30,152 --> 00:00:31,601
It's not the full story

19
00:00:31,761 --> 00:00:33,545
And if you run a business your happy

20
00:00:33,565 --> 00:00:35,739
customers are now writing your ads

21
00:00:35,759 --> 00:00:38,069
Ask them to say exactly what they loved
